From 08fbb9c31e6813499b1ea328d0de7d57eecb4099 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <backcountrymountains@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:26:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] cube: Dolby Vision FEL playback through the amstream port
 (libfelplay)

Profile 7 (FEL and MEL) goes to FelVideoRenderer, which writes Annex-B
samples (parameter sets prepended on keyframes) to /dev/amstream_dves_hevc
via libfelplay.so (JNI, source fel/felplay) so the DV driver
composes the enhancement layer. Pacing: tsync on, pts_pcrscr fed from the
player position relative to the first sample written since the last
(re)open; seeks reopen the port and use CLOSEST_SYNC. The picture is on the
video plane under the window: FEL plays use a transparent shutter and a
translucent (bufferless) SurfaceView. persist.cube.fel=0 turns it off;
debug.cube.fel.voffset_ms shifts the video clock.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
